    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe added deduplication is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Right unit.** Producing a *unique* customer code is squarely the responsibility of `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, not a separate step. The class stays single-purpose (assign the code); it isn't becoming a catch-all. `deduplicate(...)` sits alongside the existing private static `sha256Hex8(...)` helper as a second small, well-documented internal detail \u2014 exactly the shape the class already had.\n\n- **Matches established idiom.** The `for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll())` loop with the `existing.getId() != null && existing.getId().equals(owner.getId())` self-skip guard is the same pattern used verbatim in sibling steps `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` and `CountOwnerNamesakes`. Injecting `OwnerRepository` on the `service(@Val Owner owner, ...)` signature is likewise consistent with those steps. A maintainer would find this immediately familiar.\n\n- **No duplication or misplaced logic.** The base-code construction stays in `service`; only the collision-resolution concern is extracted. The helper's javadoc accurately describes its contract, and the class-level doc was updated to reflect the new behavior.\n\nNothing structural to change.",
